<h2>Source-system contract</h2><p>Use monthly schema version 2, the exact source identifier, the July 2026–June 2030 period and the <code>2030-v1</code> definitions displayed on the public goals section. Each system must explicitly approve publication. The measurement period must be a completed calendar month in the supplied timezone, followed by approval and publication timestamps. Next reporting is due through the 15th day after the following measurement month closes. Checking a connection every 15 minutes never updates a measurement or publication date.</p>
<pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"><?=e(json_encode(['schema_version'=>2,'source'=>'goblis_group','period_start'=>'2026-07-01','period_end'=>'2030-06-30','definition_version'=>'2030-v1','approved_for_publication'=>true,'publication_status'=>'approved','report_id'=>'goblis-group-2026-09','revision'=>1,'reporting_frequency'=>'monthly','measurement_period_start'=>'2026-09-01','measurement_period_end'=>'2026-09-30','measurement_timezone'=>'Africa/Nairobi','approved_at'=>'2026-10-14T09:00:00+03:00','published_at'=>'2026-10-15T09:00:00+03:00','metrics'=>['startups'=>0,'permanent_staff'=>0]],JSON_PRETTY_PRINT|JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES))?></pre>
<p>Optional fields: Ubunifu may also report <code>metrics.ubunifu_permanent_staff</code>. Any source may supply <code>metrics.indirect_beneficiaries</code>, alongside a public <code>beneficiary_basis</code> explanation and <code>beneficiary_deduplicated: true</code>. Indirect counts must exclude direct participants and document evidence of benefit; no automatic household multiplier is used. Missing optional fields leave existing feeds compatible.</p><p>The numbers above are an example, not production results. These are monthly snapshots: enterprise counts remain cumulative within the goal window, while employment is measured at month-end. Do not add monthly snapshots together. Other identifiers: <code>ubunifu</code> with <code>social_enterprises</code>; <code>afritrace</code> with <code>market_access</code>; <code>goblis_foundation</code> with its corroborating <code>market_access</code>. Send nonnegative integer aggregates only. Do not send names, identity documents, payroll details or enterprise records. Each source must deduplicate before aggregation. Schema 2 rejects unknown fields and metric keys; enterprise and person records must never be included. Older measurements, revision rollback and changed same-revision reports cannot replace the accepted report. For the same measurement month, keep the report ID and increment revision for corrections. To withdraw approval, send the same report ID/month with a higher revision, publication_status: withdrawn, approved_for_publication: false, an updated published_at, and no metrics or beneficiary fields. This removes public figures. Legacy schema 1 remains supported with its 48-hour measurement rule; it cannot replace an accepted schema 2 report.</p>
